{
  "description": [
    "The order of the Jobs page's sorts, which the master (Postgres for experiments, Go for generic tasks) and the browser must all give.",
    "Each sort: the key in the chosen direction, a missing key last in either direction, then the newest start, then the source's ID.",
    "Text (name, owner, pool): A-Z folded to a-z, compared by code point, then compared as is by code point.",
    "owner is the owner's display name. A null or empty pool is missing; end null is missing.",
    "stateGroup: PAUSED is paused; COMPLETED, CANCELED, ERROR and DELETE_FAILED are ended; any other state is active. Ascending is active, paused, ended.",
    "start and end compare at full precision (microseconds), not milliseconds.",
    "Rows are listed in ID tie-break order: when two rows tie on the key and the start, the one listed first comes first. Give them IDs in that order (experiments: a later row has a lower ID; generic tasks: a later row has a higher task ID)."
  ],
